{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Bhagu","html":"<article id='thag4.2'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 4.2 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 4.2 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catukkanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Fours </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Bhaguttheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Bhagu </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ahaṁ middhena pakato, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Overwhelmed by drowsiness, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vihārā upanikkhamiṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I left my dwelling. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Caṅkamaṁ abhiruhanto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stepping up to the path for walking meditation, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tattheva papatiṁ chamā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I fell to the ground right there. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Gattāni parimajjitvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I rubbed my limbs, and again </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>punapāruyha caṅkamaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I stepped up on the path for walking meditation. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Caṅkame caṅkamiṁ sohaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I walked meditation up and down the path, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ajjhattaṁ susamāhito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>serene inside myself. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tato me manasīkāro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Then the realization </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yoniso udapajjatha; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>came upon me—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ādīnavo pāturahu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the danger became clear, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nibbidā samatiṭṭhatha. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and I grew firmly disillusioned. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tato cittaṁ vimucci me, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Then my mind was freed—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>passa dhammasudhammataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>behold the clear rightness of the teaching! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tisso vijjā anuppattā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve attained the three knowledges, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kataṁ buddhassa sāsanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and fulfilled the Buddha’s instructions. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Bhagutthero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
